Z||000000||84fierotrevor||12-17-2001||07:17 PM||||HOW DO i GET MY KEY'S OUT ? MY DOOR'S ARE LOCKED AND i HAVE NO SPARE ! i CAN'T AFFORD A LOCK SMITH.<BR>ISN'T THERE SOME WAY TO USE A COAT HANGER ? I BEEN USING ONE IN THERE WITH A HOOK AT THE END BUT IT AINT DOING NOTHING BUT GETTING STUCK ?<BR>WHERE SHOULD i INSTERT IT ? BYE THE KEY HOLE ?<BR>HURRY ! HELP !||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroparts.com||12-17-2001||07:22 PM||||AAA<P>Or pull the glass out and have someone with a very small arm reach in and un lock it!||||reg||14
Z||000002||avengador1||12-17-2001||07:25 PM||||Do you have power locks? You could get a thin rod between the glass and gasket(make sure you put some petroleum jelly to help make it slide) and push the unlock button on the opposite side. You could also try a slim jim ( just a piece of flat stock about 1" wide and about 3 feet long) Push down between the glass and dew wipe near the lock end of the door.Wedge the glass away from the dew wipe to give better access. Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||84fierotrevor||12-17-2001||07:30 PM||||i DON'T HAVE POWER WINDOW'S AND i DON'T HAVE AAA. I HAVE A COAT HANGER. THATS ALL<BR>LOL GOD THIS SUCK'S !||||reg||1
Z||000004||84fierotrevor||12-17-2001||08:05 PM||||anyone else know ? it's dark now and i'm still trying to hook the coat hanger around that tiny little unlock knob.||||reg||1
Z||000005||California Kid||12-17-2001||08:50 PM||||HHmmmmmmmmmmmm.. Let's see, how to break into a Fiero??? Let's just post the whole routine right here, probably will save some punk thiefs some time and effort!!!!<P>Come on dudes, if your going to broadcast this type of information use the private message feature of this forum. <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||pHoOl||12-17-2001||08:51 PM||||If you have a sunroof, you might be able to pop it enough to get something in there.  I once locked my keys in the trunk and had the sunroof cracked open and was able to push some PVC in and hit the trunk release.  Good luck!!<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DJRice||12-17-2001||09:04 PM||||&lt;blonde&gt;<BR>Help.  I locked my keys in my car, the sunroof is out, the windows are down, and its about to rain!<BR>&lt;/blonde&gt;<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||avengador1||12-17-2001||09:09 PM||||You think the thieves don't know how to break in to your car? Most of them will trash your car to get in, they don't have much time to mess around. The methods I descrived above are to try and not cause any damage and were posted within the last two weeks. I'm just trying to help someone with a problem. OK?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fierobruiser||12-17-2001||09:43 PM||||I work for AAA and I can tell you,albeit a bit late, that there is nothing better than a spare $1.50 door key kept in your wallet. You don't need to call a locksmith, almost any AAA affiliated and I imagine other garages can open it for you in a about five minutes for about $30.00. If you want to open it yourself you need something less flexiible than a coat hanger.  You have to wedge something between the window and the dew wipe to sort of see what your doing. The dew wipe bracket will be in the way but you can get around it. The tool that's used is a straight rod bent 90 degrees at the bottom and then that section bent into a narrow U shape. The trick is to be able to get it around the lock slide rod and push/pull it forward. For the previous worriers about telling someone how to steal a Fiero this is no different than for almost all GM cars of the past 30 years. If a thief wants your car, locks won't stop him. Some form of electrical disablement is your best bet and maybe something like Lo-jack(sp.???) to have it recovered before it is dismantled.<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000010||Capt Fiero||12-17-2001||10:27 PM||||In a fiero that has manual windows your best bet is to get the coat hanger around the window crank and manuver the crank so the window moves down enough to get your arm in and unlock the door.  This is what I did with an 84 parts car that I had.||||reg||1
Z||000011||GTDude||12-17-2001||11:18 PM||||I know this one from experience.  Pull the window out and stuff a bunched up towel in the opening.  This should give you about 1" of space.  Take a 3 ft piece of threaded rod bent on the end and stick it in the opening.  Take the bent part and slide the door lock open.  This will open it only if you have not knocked a rod off with the clothes hanger inside the door.  God I hope you didn't.  Good luck!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||84fierotrevor||12-17-2001||11:56 PM||||I did it !!<BR>or rather the triple A guy did.<BR>My grama felt sorry for me trying for 3 hour's to get a coat hanger thrue the window and pulling the little knob, So she called her triple A to unlock it. took the guy boat 9 second's to slid this slim jim thingy in there and pop it open.<BR>oh yea anyone got soem cheap dew wipes for a 84 fiero ?<BR>mine are torn and busted cuss they where all sun bleached and cracked from the previous owner. and I tore them out the rest of the way trying to get my key's out. <BR>I need a spare key but havn't goten one made yet cuss I just got the car back from the shop since I bought it on oct 3rd. except for like 36 hour's I had it with a cracked head.<P><BR>Mentel note: get spare key's tommorow.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||84fierotrevor||12-17-2001||11:57 PM||||P.S. Thank's for everyone's help.||||reg||1
